course: dictionary
lesson: 11644
title: Arrogant
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Arrogant describes someone who behaves as if they are better or more important than other people. Think of a person who never listens and always says they are the best. That is an arrogant attitude.
explain: Look for clues in the sentence. «Mia said she didn't need to practise, because she was already the best and nobody else could ever be as good as her.» The words best and nobody else tell you that Mia thinks she is better than everyone.
explain: Arrogant is not the same as confident. A confident person believes in themselves but still respects others and is willing to listen. An arrogant person looks down on others. Ask yourself: does this person make other people feel small?
fact: Arrogant means behaving as if you are better or more important than other people.
fact: Arrogant is an adjective, so it describes a person or an attitude: an arrogant attitude, more arrogant, most arrogant.
fact: In «The Tortoise and the Hare», the hare is arrogant. He is so sure he will win that he stops to nap, and the slow tortoise wins the race.
fact: Confident means believing in yourself in a healthy way. Arrogant means thinking you are better than others.
fact: In PSHE lessons, arrogance is often compared with confidence, because confidence means believing in yourself while still respecting others.
exercise: Ruby says, «I don't need your help, I'm far cleverer than all of you.» What does this show? | *An arrogant attitude | A shy attitude | A sad attitude | A tired attitude
exercise: «The arrogant king ignored everyone who gave him advice.» Which word in this sentence describes the king? | *arrogant | king | advice | ignored
exercise: Arrogant means behaving as if you are better than other people. Which word is closest in meaning? | Shy | Gentle | *Conceited | Helpful
test: «Sam said, "I'm always right, so there's no point asking anyone else."» Is Sam being arrogant? | No, he is being shy | *Yes, he thinks he is better than others | No, he is asking for help | Yes, he is being kind
test: Which is the best example of confidence rather than arrogance? | Tom laughs at anyone who gets an answer wrong | Ella never listens to anyone's ideas | Zack says nobody in the class can beat him at anything | *Maya believes in her answer but listens when a friend shows another way
exam: Which sentence shows an arrogant attitude? | *"Everyone else is hopeless, but I'm the only one who can do this." | "I made a mistake, so I'll try again." | "Could you help me with this sum, please?" | "I'll ask my teacher, she knows more than I do."
